Provenance
----------
The default note templates are written from a description of the note style
and contain no text copied from GPL-licensed template files.

Third-party material bundled with this product
-----------------------------------------------

The theme files dracula.json, gruvbox.json, nord.json and rose-pine.json in
crates/codewiki-app/themes/ were written for CodeWiki. They use the color
values published by the palette authors named in each file's "author" and
"url" fields (Dracula, Gruvbox, Nord, Rosé Pine), whose projects are MIT
licensed.

The fonts in crates/codewiki-app/fonts/ are embedded in the desktop app,
unmodified, under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1:
Inter 4.1, Copyright 2016 The Inter Project Authors
(https://github.com/rsms/inter), license text in Inter-OFL.txt; and
JetBrains Mono 2.304, Copyright 2020 The JetBrains Mono Project Authors
(https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono), license text in
JetBrainsMono-OFL.txt.

The icons in crates/codewiki-app/icons are Material Icons by Google, licensed
under the Apache License 2.0. Their path data is taken from
@mui/icons-material 6 (MIT, Copyright (c) 2014 Call-Em-All); each file wraps
that data in an SVG element and is otherwise unmodified.

The icon bat.svg in the same folder is from Material Design Icons by
Pictogrammers (https://pictogrammers.com/library/mdi/), licensed under the
Apache License 2.0. Its path data is taken from @mdi/svg 7.4.47, wrapped the
same way.

The OpenUI Lang parser in crates/openui-lang is an independent implementation
of the language defined by https://github.com/thesysdev/openui (MIT,
Copyright Thesys Inc.). Its behavior was checked against that project's
reference parser; no source from it is included.

The folder cuda of the Windows package holds three libraries of the NVIDIA
CUDA Toolkit 13.4, unmodified: curand64_10.dll, cublas64_13.dll and
cublasLt64_13.dll. They are not part of the source of this product and are
not under its licence. They are redistributed under the NVIDIA CUDA Toolkit
End User License Agreement, whose text is in that folder as
NVIDIA-CUDA-EULA.txt (Attachment A lists them as redistributable). The worker
beside them, codewiki-embed-cuda.exe, uses them to run an embedding model on
an NVIDIA graphics card.

The embedding models CodeWiki can download are not part of this product. Each
is fetched from its publisher's repository on Hugging Face under its own
licence, Apache License 2.0 for every model of the catalog
(crates/cw-models/catalog.json).

Dependencies under the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (for example cssparser, used
by the Mermaid renderer) are used unmodified as libraries. Their source is
available from crates.io.
